    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d178">

                <pb facs="0597" n="475" sameAs="frus:frus1889/pg475"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Wharton to Sir Julian Pauncefote.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1889-07-02"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 2,
                        1889</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to your notes of the 22d of
                    May last and of the 1st ultimo, relative to the case of certain British subjects
                    who arrived on the steam-ship <hi rendition="#italic">Obdam</hi> at the port of
                    New York, where they were not allowed to land on the ground that they were
                    laborers under contract, I have the honor to inclose herewith for your
                    information a copy of a letter of the Secretary of the Treasury officially
                    reporting the action of the authorities in the premises.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William F.
                    Wharton.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d178-a1.xml" xpointer="d178-a1"/>
